# Spec 08 Phase C — kit calibration hook (PERIPHERY)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (written before implementation edits)
# C1 GIVEN a durable supplies_kit workflow response containing the ordered kit,
#    WHEN BOX_RETURN loads, THEN delivered equals the sum of small, medium,
#    large, wardrobe, and dishPack counts from that exact submitted payload.
# C2 GIVEN a nonnegative returned count, WHEN the user submits BOX_RETURN, THEN
#    users/{uid} contains the exact map kitCalibration {delivered, returned};
#    the client reads it back and only reports success when both values match.
# C3 GIVEN the optional pickup toggle is on with returned > 0, WHEN the flow
#    submits, THEN the existing requestConcierge callable creates one request
#    for BOX_RETURN with the returned count in its title; WHEN the toggle is off,
#    no concierge call is made.
# C4 GIVEN the BOX_RETURN catalog workflow id, WHEN routed, THEN a numeric,
#    nonnegative return control, optional pickup toggle, submit/error/success
#    states, and stable accessibility identifiers render; no KitEstimator
#    constant or estimation path changes.
# C5 GIVEN the Phase C diff, WHEN focused Swift tests, diff checks, a
#    fresh-context validator, and the exact iPhone 17 Pro build run, THEN C1-C4
#    receive evidence-backed PASS/FAIL before a separate Phase C commit and no
#    function, rules, catalog, vendor, or workflow deployment occurs.
#
# NEEDS-CLARIFICATION (bounded, reversible interpretations)
# - users/{uid}/kitCalibration ends at the existing user document, so
#   kitCalibration is stored as a map field on users/{uid}, not as an invalid
#   collection path without a document id.
# - delivered comes from the durable supplies_kit workflow response's submitted
#   kit JSON. That is the actual customized order and cannot drift when the
#   packing estimator later regenerates its task payload.
# - Pickup with zero returned boxes is disabled. The existing requestConcierge
#   callable is reused unchanged with taskId BOX_RETURN and category packing;
#   no backend deployment is required or permitted in this phase.
#
